{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":81,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_symm","kind":"theorem","line":873,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L873-L877","doc":"**Symmetry** `[n choose k]_q = [n choose n-k]_q` when `k ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_pos","kind":"theorem","line":866,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L866-L871","doc":"The Gaussian binomial is **positive** for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_self","kind":"theorem","line":859,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L859-L864","doc":"`[n choose n]_q = 1` (for `q > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_zero_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_zero_right","kind":"theorem","line":852,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L852-L857","doc":"`[n choose 0]_q = 1` (for `q > 1`, so `[n]_q! ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom","kind":"def","line":838,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L838-L850","doc":"The **Gaussian binomial coefficient** (q-binomial)\n`[n choose k]_q = [n]_q! / ([k]_q! · [n-k]_q!)`, in the **balanced** quantum\ninteger `[n]_q = (qⁿ−q⁻ⁿ)/(q−q⁻¹)`.\n\n**Canonical** (bean `5ldf` consolidation): this is the QOU-canonical q-binomial.\nTwo other defs exist in the tree:\n* `QOU.GaugeFieldFluidDynamics.qBinomial` — the **same** balanced object\n  (`qInteger ≡ qBracket`; verified bit-for-bit), kept as a deprecated duplicate.\n* `QOU.Machinery.QPochhammer.qBinomial` — the **standard** form\n  `(q;q)ₙ/((q;q)ₖ(q;q)_{n-k})`, a *different* normalization (e.g. `[2 choose 1]`\n  is `q+q⁻¹` here vs `1+q` there). Not interchangeable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qSchur_H2_content_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qSchur_H2_content_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":824,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L824-L831","doc":"**THEOREM (q-Schur weight at H₂).** The Markov weight of partition\nlam ⊢ 2 is y_lam = q^{c(lam)} / [2]_q. This is the bridge between the\ncontent-sum formula and the explicitly-proved H₂ weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_of_ne_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_of_ne_corner","kind":"theorem","line":768,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L768-L822","doc":"**The hook-length update rule.** Adding one box to row `r` raises the hook\nlength by exactly one on two sets of cells and leaves every other cell alone:\n\n* the cells of row `r` strictly left of the new box (their **arm** grows);\n* the cells of column `λ_r` strictly above row `r` (their **leg** grows).\n\nThe new box itself, `(r, λ_r)`, is excluded: its hook length in the new shape is\n`1` only because no row below `r` exceeds `λ_r`, which is the weakly-decreasing\nproperty — and `Partition` is a bare `List ℕ` that does not carry it. Stating\nthe rule off the corner keeps it unconditional; the corner is supplied\nseparately by whatever carries the order hypothesis.\n\nThis is the per-cell input to the Pieri step of the Macdonald hook telescope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxNewRow_mem_addableCorners","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxNewRow_mem_addableCorners","kind":"theorem","line":760,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L760-L766","doc":"**The new bottom row is always a corner**, and it is always the last one\nlisted. Recorded because the `++ [addBoxNewRow lam]` is easy to drop when\nrefactoring, and `addableCorners` would then silently under-enumerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_three_two_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_three_two_one","kind":"theorem","line":757,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L757-L758","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_two_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_two_two","kind":"theorem","line":755,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L755-L755","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_two_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_two_one","kind":"theorem","line":752,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L752-L753","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners_one","kind":"theorem","line":750,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L750-L750","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addableCorners","kind":"def","line":736,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L736-L742","doc":"The shapes obtained from `lam` by adding one box at an addable corner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxNewRow_example","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxNewRow_example","kind":"theorem","line":718,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L718-L723","doc":"Concrete check, matching the probe: `[3,2,1] ++ [1] = [3,2,1,1]`, and\n`n` goes `4 → 7` because the new row sits at index `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxNewRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxNewRow","kind":"theorem","line":705,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L705-L716","doc":"**`n(λ ++ [1]) = n(λ) + ℓ(λ)`**: the new row sits at index `ℓ(λ)` and holds\none cell, so it contributes exactly its own index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxNewRow_new_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxNewRow_new_cell","kind":"theorem","line":693,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L693-L703","doc":"**The new cell's hook length is `1`, unconditionally.** Nothing lies below\nthe last row, so no order hypothesis is needed — unlike the interior corner,\nwhich `hookLength_addBoxRow_of_ne_corner` has to exclude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxNewRow_col_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxNewRow_col_zero","kind":"theorem","line":679,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L679-L691","doc":"**Column `0` gains exactly one**, for every row of `lam` that has a cell\nthere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxNewRow_col_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxNewRow_col_pos","kind":"theorem","line":662,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L662-L677","doc":"**Only column `0` moves.** The new row holds a single cell, so its entry `1`\nexceeds `j` exactly when `j = 0`; for every other column the leg count is blind\nto it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.drop_addBoxNewRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.drop_addBoxNewRow","kind":"theorem","line":655,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L655-L660","doc":"The tail below row `i` gains the new row, for any `i` inside `lam`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxNewRow_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxNewRow_self","kind":"theorem","line":648,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L648-L653","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxNewRow_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxNewRow_lt","kind":"theorem","line":643,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L643-L646","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.length_addBoxNewRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.length_addBoxNewRow","kind":"theorem","line":637,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L637-L641","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxNewRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxNewRow","kind":"def","line":634,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L634-L635","doc":"Add a box as a **new bottom row** of one cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxRow_at_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxRow_at_length","kind":"theorem","line":628,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L628-L632","doc":"**The trap, stated as a theorem** so it cannot be re-discovered by accident:\nadding a box \"at row `lam.length`\" via `addBoxRow` does nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxRow_row_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxRow_row_zero","kind":"theorem","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L611-L612","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxRow_row_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxRow_row_one","kind":"theorem","line":608,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L608-L609","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_addBoxRow","kind":"theorem","line":588,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L588-L600","doc":"**`n(λ + box in row r) = n(λ) + r`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":573,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L573-L586","doc":"**`n(λ + box in row r) = n(λ) + r`.**\n\n`n(λ) = Σ_i i·λ_i`, so raising `λ_r` by one adds exactly `r`. This is the\nprefactor's share of the Pieri step: `schurElement`'s `Q^{n(λ)}` becomes\n`Q^{n(λ)+r}` when the box goes into row `r`, and nothing else about the\nprefactor moves.\n\nNote the direction of the dependence: the increment is the ROW INDEX, not the\nrow length. A box added to row `0` does not change `n(λ)` at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxRow_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxRow_ne","kind":"theorem","line":559,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L559-L563","doc":"Every other row is untouched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxRow_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.getElem?_addBoxRow_self","kind":"theorem","line":553,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L553-L557","doc":"The row that received the box is one cell longer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.length_addBoxRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.length_addBoxRow","kind":"theorem","line":546,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L546-L551","doc":"Adding a box does not change the number of rows (`List.set` does not). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_row_above_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_row_above_ne","kind":"theorem","line":529,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L529-L544","doc":"**Rows above the new box, off its column, are untouched.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_leg_growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_leg_growth","kind":"theorem","line":505,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L505-L527","doc":"**Leg growth.** For a cell in column `λ_r` strictly above row `r`, the hook\nlength increases by exactly one: the arm is untouched (the row entry at `i` is\nnot the one that moved) and the leg count crosses its threshold.\n\nThe hypothesis `λ_r < λ_i` is what puts the cell inside `λ` in the first place;\nwithout it both sides are `0` and there is nothing to say. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_drop_addBoxRow_off_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_drop_addBoxRow_off_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":483,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L483-L503","doc":"**Off the threshold the leg count does not move.** For a row `i` above the\nnew box and any column `j ≠ λ_r`, raising `λ_r` to `λ_r + 1` does not change\nwhether row `r` exceeds `j`: below the threshold both exceed it, above it\nneither does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_set_of_same","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_set_of_same","kind":"theorem","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L467-L481","doc":"**Setting one entry to another with the same `p`-value leaves the count\nalone.** The companion to `countP_set_of_flip`: together they say the count\nmoves by exactly the indicator of a flip. Also proved by structural induction —\nMathlib carries no `countP`-over-`set` lemma reachable from here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_drop_addBoxRow_at_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_drop_addBoxRow_at_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L442-L465","doc":"**Leg growth, as a count.** For a row `i` strictly above the new box, the\ntail below `i` still contains row `r`, whose entry moves from `λ_r` to `λ_r + 1`.\nAt the threshold `j = λ_r` that flips the predicate `(· > j)` from false to true,\nso the leg count rises by exactly one.\n\nThis is the half the `drop` argument cannot reach: the modified entry survives\ninto the tail rather than being dropped, so the proof is a `countP`-over-`set`\nargument instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_set_of_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.countP_set_of_flip","kind":"theorem","line":426,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L426-L440","doc":"**Setting one entry from a value failing `p` to one satisfying it raises the\ncount by exactly one.** The counting step behind leg growth; proved by\nstructural induction rather than found in Mathlib. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_row_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_row_below","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L413-L424","doc":"**Rows strictly below the new box are untouched.** For `r < i` the row entry\nis unchanged (the `set` is at a different index) and so is the tail, so the hook\nlength is literally the same. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_same_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.hookLength_addBoxRow_same_row","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L389-L411","doc":"**Arm growth.** For a cell of row `r` strictly left of the new box, the hook\nlength increases by exactly one.\n\nThe leg is unchanged by `drop_addBoxRow`; the arm goes from `λ_r − j − 1` to\n`λ_r − j`, which is `+1` precisely because `j < λ_r` (this is `ℕ` subtraction,\nso the hypothesis is doing real work, not decoration). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.drop_addBoxRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.drop_addBoxRow","kind":"theorem","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L381-L387","doc":"**The tail below row `i` is untouched** whenever the box goes in at or above\n`i` — `List.set` at index `r ≤ i` is invisible after `drop (i+1)`. This is what\nkeeps the *leg* fixed in the arm-growth case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.addBoxRow","kind":"def","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L377-L379","doc":"Add one box to row `r`. Out of range, this is the identity (`List.set` is). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_ne_contentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_ne_contentSum","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L351-L355","doc":"**`n(λ)` and `contentSum` are genuinely different**, witnessed at `λ = (1,1)`:\n`n(λ) = 1` but `contentSum λ = −1`. Stated so the confusion cannot recur\nsilently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_three_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_three_one","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L349-L349","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_one_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_one_one","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L348-L348","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_two","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L347-L347","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda_nil","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L339-L341","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda","kind":"def","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L333-L337","doc":"**`n(λ) = Σ_i i · λ_i`** (0-indexed rows), the row-weighted size of a\npartition. This is the standard `n(λ)` of Macdonald I.1, written for\n0-indexed rows so that `n(λ) = Σ_{i≥0} i·λ_i` rather than `Σ_{i≥1}(i−1)λ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_one_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_one_one","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L319-L320","doc":"Content sum of (1,1) = -1 (cells at (0,0) and (1,0)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_two","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L316-L317","doc":"Content sum of (2) = 1 (cells at (0,0) and (0,1)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_one","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L312-L314","doc":"Content sum of (1) = 0 (single cell at (0,0)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum_nil","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L308-L310","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.contentSum","kind":"def","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L301-L306","doc":"Content sum c(lam) = Σ_{(i,j)∈lam} (j - i).\nSum of contents over all cells in the Young diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.cellContent","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L298-L299","doc":"Content of a cell at position (i, j) in a Young diagram: j - i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qDim_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qDim_nil","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L293-L296","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qDim","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L278-L291","doc":"The **q-deformed dimension** of partition `lam ⊢ n`:\n\n  dim_q(lam) = [n]_q! / ∏_{x ∈ lam} [h_x]_q.\n\nComputed as a fold over rows × columns, using\n`Partition.hookLength` for each cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.hookLength_outside_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.hookLength_outside_nil","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L269-L272","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.length_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.length_nil","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L266-L267","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.size_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.size_nil","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L263-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.hookLength","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L246-L261","doc":"**Hook length** at cell `(i, j)` (0-indexed) of partition `lam`,\nwhen `(i, j) ∈ lam`.  For cells outside `lam`, returns 0.\n\n`h(i, j) = arm(i, j) + leg(i, j) + 1` where\n  `arm(i, j) = lam_i - j - 1`  (cells to the right in row i)\n  `leg(i, j) = |{ i' > i : lam_{i'} > j }|`  (cells below in col j) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.conjugate","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L237-L244","doc":"The **conjugate** (transpose) partition `lam'`.\n\nConvention: for each column index `j ∈ [0, maxPart lam)`, the\nconjugate part is the number of rows with at least `j + 1`\nboxes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.maxPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.maxPart","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L234-L235","doc":"The maximal row length (= number of columns in the conjugate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.length","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L231-L232","doc":"The number of rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition.size","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L228-L229","doc":"The size `|lam| = Σ lam_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.Partition","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L221-L224","doc":"A **partition** as a list `lam = [lam_1, lam_2, …]` of positive parts.\nNo order constraint is imposed at the type level; downstream\nstructure theorems may assume weakly decreasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L214-L217","doc":"For `q > 1`, `[n]_q!` is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_pos","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L204-L212","doc":"For `q > 1`, the q-factorial `[n]_q! > 0` for any `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L199-L202","doc":"For `q > 1` and `n ≥ 1`, the q-bracket `[n]_q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_pos","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L189-L197","doc":"For `q > 1` and `n ≥ 1`, the q-bracket `[n]_q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.q_pow_dom_inv_at_q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.q_pow_dom_inv_at_q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L162-L187","doc":"For `q > 1`, `q^n > q^(-n)` whenever `n ≥ 1`.\n\n**Proof**: For `q > 1` and `n ≥ 1`, `q^n > 1` (one_lt_pow₀), so\n`(q^n)⁻¹ < 1 < q^n`; rewrite `q^(-n) = (q^n)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.q_sub_q_inv_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.q_sub_q_inv_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L158-L160","doc":"The Hecke deformation is nonzero for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.q_sub_q_inv_pos_at_q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.q_sub_q_inv_pos_at_q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L137-L156","doc":"The Hecke deformation `q − q⁻¹` is positive when `q > 1`.\n\n**Proof**: For `q > 1`, we have `0 < q`, and since `q⁻¹ · q = 1`\nwith `q⁻¹ > 0`, we get `q⁻¹ < 1 < q`, hence `q − q⁻¹ > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_succ","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L132-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial_zero","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L129-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qFactorial","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L122-L127","doc":"The **q-factorial** `[n]_q! = ∏_{k=1}^n [k]_q`.\n\nEmpty product convention: `[0]_q! = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_add","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L107-L120","doc":"**Balanced quantum-integer addition identity** `[a+b]_q = q^b·[a]_q + q^{-a}·[b]_q`.\nThe defining relation behind the q-Pascal rule for the Gaussian binomial (and hence the\nRogers–Szegő / continuous q-Hermite three-term recurrence). Verified at the formula level:\n`q^b(q^a−q^{-a}) + q^{-a}(q^b−q^{-b}) = q^{a+b} − q^{-a-b}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_eq_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_eq_formula","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L98-L105","doc":"**The if-guard is redundant: the closed formula already vanishes at `n = 0`.**\n`qBracket q n = (q^n − q^{-n}) / (q − q⁻¹)` for *every* `n` (at `n = 0` both sides are\n`0`), so downstream proofs may use the uniform formula without case-splitting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_two","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L81-L96","doc":"**`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`** when `q ≠ 0` and the denominator is nonzero.\n\nProved via difference of squares:\n  `(q² − q⁻²) = (q − q⁻¹)(q + q⁻¹)`,\nthen `mul_div_cancel_left₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_one","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L72-L79","doc":"**`[1]_q = 1` whenever the denominator is well-defined.**\n\nProved directly: `(q^1 - q^(-1)) / (q - q⁻¹) = (q - q⁻¹)/(q - q⁻¹) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_zero","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L68-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L55-L66","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket.**  The `n = 0` guard is\nredundant — `qIntBal q 0 = (1 − 1)/(q − q⁻¹) = 0` already — so the agreement is\nunconditional, on the degenerate locus too.  The `def` is kept because\n`qFactorial` and the `1 < q` positivity lemmas below unfold it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBracket","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPartitionCombinatorics.lean#L48-L53","doc":"The **q-bracket** `[n]_q = (q^n − q^{-n}) / (q − q⁻¹)` for `n : ℕ`.\nAt `n = 0` we set `[0]_q := 0`; for `n ≥ 1` the formula reduces to\n`1 + q² + q⁴ + … + q^{2(n−1)}` (up to a `q^{-(n-1)}` factor). ","signatureChunk":0}]}